<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peroz I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 459–484</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peroz I was a Sasanian king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> who reigned from 459 to 484. He took the throne from his brother Hormizd III with Hephthalite help, drove the Kidarites from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> around 467 and endured a severe famine. He was twice defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a>, once being captured and ransomed, and was killed fighting them in 484, after which Persia paid them tribute.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peroz-i.jpg" alt="Peroz I" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hermitage Museum · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plate_of_Peroz_I_hunting.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
